    notes: "One is right. The provider holds nothing between calls — the whole conversation goes up with every request, which is why the list IS the memory and why forgetting to append leaves the model with no idea it ever spoke. Land the sting in the small print: the two plausible-sounding wrong answers claim a benefit, and the truth is the exact opposite. Every turn you keep costs you again. That is the thread back to pattern 4 — summarising is not tidying, it is cost control."
