    notes: "Three is right, and four is worth a moment because it is a genuinely widespread misunderstanding: nothing is learned from a conversation. The model is not improving as you talk to it — it is re-reading the same growing pile of text on each call, which costs more tokens and takes longer. Both curves go the wrong way together. This is the whole economic argument for pattern 4: recent turns verbatim, older ones summarised, and the bulk of what you know kept outside the conversation in a store you query."
