    notes: "Three is right, and this is the single best argument for pattern 7 in the whole deck, so give it room. The other three answers are the ones an engineer reaches for — crashes, latency, cost — and none of them is the thing that gets you fired. What makes this example land is that the agent is not broken and has not been jailbroken: it was told to reply to the email, sending is how replying completes, and it completed. That is precisely why the gate cannot live in the prompt. You cannot instruct your way out of an agent doing exactly what you asked. Ask the room which tool in their own system would be dangerous under that reading; someone always names one they had not thought about."
