    notes: "Two is right. Handing the cleanup back with the subscription is a small design choice with a big payoff: the caller cannot forget where the off switch is, because they were given it. Skip it and listeners accumulate — each holding whatever it closed over — which in a long-lived server is a slow leak that looks like a mystery until someone profiles it. Worth naming the general habit: whatever acquires a resource should hand back the way to release it, in the same breath."
