    notes: "Two is right. The shape of an event log is the point: the fields you filter and sort on — run id, event type, timestamp, sequence number — are proper columns, and the payload, which is different for every event type, is one JSON column. That way you get real queries over the structure without inventing forty nullable columns for forty event types. One is the trap and worth killing: a JSON column enforces that the value is valid JSON and nothing more. If you want the payload to match a schema, that check is yours to write — which is the same lesson as the tool input schema, one layer down."
